+  // 2 · a house curve read becomes its own token (B8 reads it); any OTHER var() with a
+  //     time fallback is a LOCAL (--draw-dur), ruled at its own site.
+  masked = masked.replace(OTHER_VAR, (_m, name, fb) => {
+    // A HOUSE CURVE IS EITHER LAYER'S (pass 4, the §13 fold). `--ease-*` is T6's shape
+    // vocabulary; `--verb-*-ease` is MOT-VERB's timing layer and it is the form the estate
+    // ships now. B8 read only the first, so every verb-eased transition on the merged tree
+    // read as "NO curve … the UA's own `ease` by omission" — 50 false reds, the whole of
+    // this lane's exit 1. Both prefixes are a house curve here; which LAYER a curve belongs
+    // to is `lint:verbs`' question, not this gate's.
